---
id: butter-glazed-argentine-shrimp
title: Butter-Glazed Garlic & Lemon Argentine Shrimp
category: modular_protein

yield:
  servings: 1
  cooked_g: 175

storage:
  fridge_days: 3
  freezer_friendly: false

---

Place @argentine-red-shrimp{227%g} in a colander under gentle cold running water for ~thaw-time{4%min} until completely pliable.

Peel off the shells along the pre-split back and remove the tail fans. Pat the shrimp thoroughly dry on all sides using paper towels (removing all surface moisture is essential for a high-heat sear rather than boiling in purge).

Toss the dried shrimp with @kosher-salt{0.125%tsp}, @black-pepper{0.25%tsp}, and @smoked-paprika{0.25%tsp}.

Heat a dry non-stick #skillet over medium-high heat until hot. Lay shrimp in a single flat layer with space between pieces. Sear undisturbed for ~sear-side-one{90%sec}. Flip and sear for ~sear-side-two{45%sec} until flesh turns opaque white-pink and curls into a loose C-shape (do not overcook into a tight O-shape).

Turn off the burner completely (or remove skillet from heat). Immediately add @unsalted-butter{0.5%tbsp}, finely minced @fresh-garlic{1%clove}, and juice squeezed from @fresh-lemon{0.5} directly into the pan. Swirl and toss continuously for ~glaze-time{20%sec} as residual pan heat melts the butter into a glossy emulsion with lemon juice without scorching garlic or milk solids.

Transfer immediately into a meal prep container (175 g cooked yield) and spoon the lemon-butter pan glaze over the top.
